														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4056217">
									

<p>I'm upvoting because this is written very well, and the dialogue is great, but I don't feel like much <em>happens</em>. I clicked that Nobody link, and I imagine that if I read that tale I would get some good context for this piece, but as is it just doesn't hit many notable&#8230; notes.</p>
<p>We have a sphere that gives people powers, and clearly attempts to touch as many people as possible, and we have it set in a broken masquerade scenario, and the link (and tags) tell me that Nobody is involved. The most mystery we really get let onto is the fact that he feels like there's a hole in his head when he thinks about the sphere&#8230;</p>
<p>But that plot point feels like the <em>beginning</em> of a big mystery, and this is certainly written to feel like it sets that up, but instead it ends then and there. I'm left wanting more, but not in a good way. And thus&#8230; well, still upvote, because damn you're good at dialogue, but you know. I felt the need to leave a comment.</p>

							</div>

								
					
